# Scope of the committed code graph. `graphify update .` -- what the
# `graphify-update` hook and the weekly `graphify.yml` workflow both run -- has
# no `--code-only` flag, and the scope `graphify extract --code-only` used is
# kept in a gitignored cache. So the scope has to live here, or a rebuild in a
# fresh clone silently indexes ~950 extra nodes and the graph stops being
# reproducible. Everything below is what `--code-only` skipped.

# Prose, papers and images: no code, and extracting them wants an LLM, so they
# would make the graph depend on whether the builder has an API key.
*.md
*.tex
*.bib
*.pdf
*.png

# Not source: 40-odd near-identical CD workflows contributed a quarter of the
# graph's nodes as bare YAML keys ("description", "required", "value"), which
# bloats the committed graph and pollutes query results.
.github/
